WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.946
[EDDIE HARRIS, "FREEDOM JAZZ
 DANCE"]

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:33.160
The overarching theme is social
equality, police brutality,

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.080
media, news
propaganda, the things

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.000
that we unfortunately
have to see,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.670
it feels to me as a Black
man day in and day out.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.020
It really weighs
on me and bugs me

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.960
that I have to keep
addressing the same thing.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.060
People think, oh, you're
living your dreams,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.310
traveling the world and stuff.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.000
It's true.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.990
But I really would like to just
write love poems if I could.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.750
But the reality is,
like Nina Simone said,

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.110
you have the artist's duty
is to reflect the times.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.320
I've watched war commence
on colored kids who

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.070
wither like acres of
daffodils anchored in bodies

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.230
of bloody water where
the deceased are greeted

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.660
with the deep indifference.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.140
I've witnessed temperamental
white teams being

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.840
tamed with tasers but Black
babies with empty hands

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.060
oftentimes pacified
with gunfire.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.940
[BEATBOXING]

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.540
I've even seen people pull their
phones from pockets and purses

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.580
like pistols to shoot
indisputable proof.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:44.310
But Facebook footage is never a
footprint for indictment here.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.570
The reality is hands
up or not, gunshots

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.476
turn our torsos into hashtags.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.090
Therefore, we reformat
tribute tweets

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.680
in an attempt to
retract that trauma.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.840
But that trick is
never a treatment

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.670
for our trail of
tears, especially when,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:08.550
especially when,
especially when--

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.509
I do feel like we're
making progress.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:12.070
But we have a long ways to go.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.580
So if something I'm
saying strikes a chord

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.070
or resonates with a
student, just one,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.450
I feel like my job is done.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.210
Because that student
can go on to change

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.210
the course of the world.

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.252
[JET LEWIS, "UNLEARNING HOW TO
 SAVE THE PLANET"]

00:02:24.252 --> 00:02:25.890
It's hard to break
into this field

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:29.610
when the first thing everyone
notices about you is your race.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:30.750
Look at my face.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:35.120
Why can't I also
inhabit this space?

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.660
There's diversity in
the birds and the trees.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.800
But we have not figured out how
to guarantee the same diversity

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.260
in the kinds of people
that want to protect them.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.960
We are all looking to do sort of
this broad-reaching conception

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.560
of thought through sound to
be able to reach the listener

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.460
and help conjure up images
of the difficulty of living

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.130
in this time period,
but also the hope that's

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:04.280
coupled with it, in order to
gain a deeper understanding

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.150
and empathy.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:08.000
These words, and the music,
and all of these things

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.460
that we're dealing
with are just a means

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.080
of trying to
communicate a better

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.693
way of being with one another.

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:15.610
[SEAN JONES, "PANGEA"]

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:39.480
The harmonies of all
things resonating as one.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.229
[TERRI LYNE CARRINGTON,
"SEEN/UNSEEN--

00:04:03.229 --> 00:04:05.217
EXPLORATIONS, INTERROGATIONS,
AND RESILIENCE"]

00:04:05.217 --> 00:04:08.696
[VOCALIZATIONS]

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.670
The piece centers around the
resilience of Black women

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.840
to imagine what it's like
being born as a Black woman

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.860
into a world that's
pretty unjust to you.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:54.840
Just how we've had
to navigate through.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:05:01.670
So many things and
really always emerge

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:06.650
still hopeful, and still
joyful, and all of the emotions,

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.760
and all of the things
that just go along

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.095
with a certain kind of struggle.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:10.250
And it's always great to see
someone as vibrant as Fred.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.860
His conducting style is unique.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:13.940
It's very energetic.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:14.630
He's moving.

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:18.230
He's sort of in the moment,
picking different pieces

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.922
of this and this.

00:07:19.922 --> 00:07:22.520
And I think that
that's really important

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:27.140
to have someone that is rooted
in the traditions of conducting

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:29.510
while being so experimental.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.902
[BEATBOXING]

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:35.320
The main thing is to be as
honest as possible musically

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.230
really.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:40.270
Situations like this are
a really good opportunity

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:43.059
to, I think, step outside
of one's comfort zone,

00:08:43.059 --> 00:08:45.820
especially when
collaborating with others

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:48.190
and being given an
opportunity to share

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:51.760
your sort of musical
voice and identity

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.959
in a way that adds to
someone else's vision.

00:08:53.959 --> 00:08:55.292
[BRAXTON COOK, "LOST AND FOUND"]

00:08:55.292 --> 00:08:57.580
Reimagining this
American-made playing field

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.410
built to kill my kind on sight.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:05.860
But the way I see it, the way I
see it, we don't look the part

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:08.260
or fit the picturesque
European picture

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:11.150
frame the same as Mona Lisa.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.950
See, our beauty be different.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:18.020
Be curly, be kinky, be cornrows
on corn bread-fed fingers.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:21.900
Cut the serve face flawless.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.880
We dictate the
market masterfully,

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:28.780
supplying the demand for
culture will trends appropriated

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:31.100
on countless occasions.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.530
Yet somehow, we innovate.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:33.340
We innovate.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.270
We innovate to no end.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.180
I feature this
spoken word artist

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.790
that I think is really able
to put all of the themes

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.593
that the song is
about into words

00:09:41.593 --> 00:09:44.260
and communicate that in the most
powerful poignant way possible.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.100
His name is Orlando Watson.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:48.100
And then, I'm also featuring
Andrew Renfroe, one

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.270
of my best friends, guitarist.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.395
We went to school together.

00:09:50.395 --> 00:09:53.920
And they're just integral to
getting the message across.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:58.860
Kingdom come to make amends,
recompense for sins against

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:05.706
People of the sun whose peace,
whose peace, whose peace,

00:10:05.706 --> 00:10:10.690
whose peace is still
as it used to be.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.940
Peace ain't promise, Your Honor.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:17.160
Let's be honest and
acknowledge that.

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.150
It must be now.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:24.800
[APPLAUSE]

